[Themes "c4-space,quick-development"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "2...Nf6"]
[Start "qa5-classical 2.exd5"]

2... Nf6 3. d4 { Takes the centre at once. If Black takes back on d5 with the knight, c4 comes with a tempo. } 3... Nxd5 ( 3... g6 4. c4 ) ( 3... Bg4 4. Nf3 Bxf3 5. Qxf3 ) ( 3... c6 4. dxc6 Nxc6 5. Nf3 ) ( 3... Qxd5 4. Nc3 { Develops with an attack on the queen. After ...Qa5, ...Qd6 or ...Qd8 the game is the same as 2...Qxd5 3.Nc3 with ...Nf6 and d4 added. } ) 4. c4 { Kicks the knight away and builds a big pawn centre. It leaves a hole on d4, but White's pieces will cover it. } 4... Nb6 ( 4... Nb4 5. a3 N4c6 6. Nf3 ) ( 4... Nf6 5. Nc3 { Develops and guards d5 and e4. Plan: Nf3, Be2 and castling, with more space in the centre. } ) 5. Nf3 { Develops and defends d4 so the centre pawns stay put. } 5... Bg4 6. Be2 { Gets ready to castle and keeps h3 in reserve if the bishop takes on f3. } 6... e6 7. Nc3 { Brings out the last knight to guard the centre. Plan: castle, then d5 or c5 to gain space. } 7... Nc6 8. O-O Be7 9. h3 { Asks the bishop the same question: trade on f3 or retreat. } *
